{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch7JdRnpyxFB2HQydYTCm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The Majestic's refund last time is the strongest point in this pitch. You already returned every dollar once, so the all-or-nothing promise is one people know you'll keep. I put it in the open.\n\n<final_document>\n**Bring Back the Majestic**\n\nThe screen at the Majestic on Main Street has been dark since 2022. Our town has 6,500 people, and the nearest cinema is now 38 miles away. Seeing a film on a Friday night means a 76-mile round trip.\n\nWhen the Majestic closed, it was still selling about 180 tickets a week. The audience never left. Now we have a real chance to reopen it.\n\n**What it takes**\n\nWe need $85,000 to replace the projector and sound system and to fix the roof. If we raise it, the building's owner will rent the Majestic to us for $1 a year for ten years.\n\n**Where we stand**\n\n- A local bank has pledged $25,000 if we raise the rest by June 30, 2027.\n- Three local businesses have already pledged $11,000 in writing.\n- 46 volunteers have signed up to run the box office and the snack bar.\n\nThe rest has to come from us: the people who live here and want our cinema back.\n\n**Yes, we've tried before**\n\nThree years ago we set out to raise $120,000. We reached $47,000, fell short, and returned every pledge in full.\n\nThis time the goal is $35,000 lower. The bank and local businesses are already on board. And the promise is the same: this campaign is all-or-nothing. If we don't reach $85,000 by June 30, 2027, every pledge comes back to you in full. We've done it before, and you can hold us to it.\n\n**What we're asking**\n\nPledge what you can, then tell a neighbor, your family group chat, and whoever you used to see at the Saturday matinee. Every dollar from this town also unlocks the bank's $25,000.\n\nLet's turn the lights back on at the Majestic.\n</final_document>\n\nAbout 300 words. Three things to settle before you publish:\n\n- **The amount still needed.** Your figures don't fit together yet, so the pitch says \"the rest\" and gives no number. $85,000 minus the bank's $25,000 is $60,000. If the businesses' $11,000 counts toward that, the public needs to raise $49,000. If the public really needs $60,000 on top of the businesses' $11,000, the total is $96,000, not $85,000. Tell me which is right and I'll add the exact figure. Backers give more readily when they know how much is left.\n- **The roof estimate.** It's from last fall and could rise by up to 15%. I left it out of the pitch because I don't know how you'd cover the extra. If the price goes up after people have pledged, tell them straight away. You could also decide now whether to aim a little above $85,000 as a cushion.\n- **\"The Saturday matinee.\"** I invented that detail as a nod to past regulars. Swap it for something real if you have one, or cut it."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":980,"cache_read_input_tokens":9876,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":980},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"32a829cd-a10c-4e72-8ba5-629b167a2a63","uuid":"dc2bbb23-c2fa-4579-ab22-71e9ad406eb0","timestamp":"2026-11-16T21:19:33.241Z","request_id":"req_011Ch7JdRavYeSJbL2m8frG5"}
